+# Turn 7 remains: exact completed subproblem and the next indispensable arrow
+
+## Completed here
+
+The supplied audit asked whether its original odd-receiver numerator N=S^6 F
+can vanish at a positive integral hard-prime ES witness. It cannot: N<-c p^8
+for every prime p=1 mod12, with the two explicit constants in the proof.
+The result is not confined to the audit's three negative-character classes.
+The original inverse exists with norm <360 S^9/(c p^8), including the actual
+root/sign labels and unchanged external metric factors.
+
+Do not re-prove local exclusions of F=0 or assume that increasing p-adic
+precision in the remaining character classes will prove this result. The
+new proof is global arithmetic: u>=2 (>=5 in the mod24 class), and integral
+middle tail gap c-b>=1. Both have complete positive polynomial certificates.
+The coefficient checks prove universal identities using degree bounds, while
+the prime census only compares two state enumeration implementations.
+
+## Still unproved
+
+For every prescribed hard prime, existence of an original state in the complete
+E/M divisor atlas. Neither the determinant bound nor invertibility of a
+receiving map supplies that first state. The explicit raw E source at
+p1009,a321,R275,u9 already has nonzero determinant but fails its full gate.
+The preceding exact residual-divisor descent and its nine-word theorem remain
+valid within their stated domains; their initial-source problem was not solved
+by this continuation.
+
+## Useful next work
+
+A determinant-based attempt must now produce an arithmetic source or a lower
+bound for an original occupied coefficient, using information independent of
+the receiver's mere invertibility. Its lost denominator/gate data must be
+retained. Alternatively continue the same-prime source-changing arithmetic
+rather than optimizing this now-complete nonvanishing subproblem.
+
+## Permanent controls
+
+- Positive real, simple-root ES quartics can have F=0. The t,t+1/10 family
+  changes sign; real positivity cannot replace the integer tail gap.
+- Exact p-adic zeros in the audit are compatible with the global theorem.
+- N nonzero does not mean p does not divide N; M v_p(N)=2 occurs.
+- The three old character tests are sufficient antecedents, not necessary
+  conditions for an actual integral witness's frame to be invertible.
+- The literal quartic, reciprocal cubic and root-order conductors are different
+  objects. No seven/eight-branch count or integral lattice is silently changed.
+- Do not call this a completed witness-guaranteed Turn 8 algorithm.
